    "title": "XR prize rank-one trade flat/basis owner",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For a rank-one trade, two active slopes force both received directions to restrict into W on the whole common dual support S. If S spans W, its first basis is shared by every active block, the remaining support is persistent for that basis pencil, and the active population is at most floor((R-v)/h). If rank_W(S)=j<a, its closure is a proper flat of size at most j+u, which requires u>=1. This is a canonical owner dichotomy, not an aggregate count.",
